-ImagePath "{DRIVE}\images"

:: ---------------------------------------------------------------------
:: HOW THIS FILE WORKS
:: ---------------------------------------------------------------------
:: startnet.cmd reads only the FIRST LINE of this file (via `set /p`)
:: and passes it verbatim to unified_winpe_deploy.ps1. Everything after
:: line 1 - including these `::` comment lines and blank lines - is
:: silently ignored. Do NOT put commentary on line 1 or the shipped
:: default becomes broken PowerShell input.
::
:: To switch profiles: DELETE the line 1 default above and paste one of
:: the examples below onto line 1 (drop its leading `::` prefix). Edit
:: paths, disk numbers, PIN, etc. for your USB, then save.
::
:: Verbatim copy of this file gives you the safe interactive default:
:: WIM lookup pre-set to {DRIVE}\images, everything else prompted at
:: the WinPE console.
::
:: ---------------------------------------------------------------------
:: EXAMPLE 1 - Single-ISO workflow (build_iso.ps1 output, one file, Rufus to USB)
:: {DRIVE} is substituted at boot time with the drive letter WinPE
:: assigns the USB. build_iso.ps1 writes this file automatically; edit
:: before building if you want a different profile.
:: ---------------------------------------------------------------------
:: -WimFile "{DRIVE}\images\Win11_Pro_Custom.wim" -TargetDisk 0 -UnattendFile "{DRIVE}\configs\unattend.xml" -Force -Silent
::
:: ---------------------------------------------------------------------
:: EXAMPLE 2 - Two-partition USB (legacy: FAT32 WinPE boot + NTFS IMAGES data partition)
:: Drive letter is fixed at whatever letter the IMAGES partition gets
:: (I: below is an example - substitute your own).
:: ---------------------------------------------------------------------
:: -WimFile "I:\images\Win11_Enterprise.wim" -TargetDisk 0 -UnattendFile "I:\configs\unattend.xml" -DataDiskNumber 1 -EnableBitLocker -BitLockerPin "ReplaceWithYourPin42" -Force -Silent
